ict.<br /> <br /> Not sure about your initial question though. Lots of Anime are very different. I think it'd do a pretty good job of portraying something like Princess Mononoke, or Spirited Away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:55:27-07:00","id":979080,"title":"","content":"With all its focus on myth and legend, I also think in some ways that Scion could potentially be a good match for a Fate/Stay Night game.<br /> <br /> Reading over the rules, I feel like the Storypath system would be a great fit for running the type of high action games designed to emulate shounen anime/manga. If we ever just got a generic Storypath system core book, I would personally love to hack it into a One Piece setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:06:28-07:00","id":979089,"title":"","content":"I think Exalted is the Anime RPG system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435